# Trailing-slash forms of the legacy WordPress URLs.
#
# WordPress published every one of these with a trailing slash, so that is the
# form Google has indexed and the form a real visitor clicks. Astro strips the
# slash when it generates its own rules from astro.config.mjs, which left the
# indexed form unmatched. Cloudflare reads the first matching line, so these sit
# above the generated ones and both forms now answer with a 301.
#
# Do not delete. Without them every ranking page 404s.

